---
import NoteFigure from './NoteFigure.astro';
---

<NoteFigure
  label="Coupling layer"
  title="Keep one group, transform the other, then reverse the same operations"
  caption="Reconstructed from the affine coupling equations and block Jacobian on pages 35–36. The conditioner receives only uₐ, so the unchanged output vₐ supplies the same parameters for the inverse. Explicit inverse arrows and network-reuse annotations are editorial additions. All products and exponentials are elementwise; finite real log scales give nonzero scales in exact arithmetic."
>
  <div class="coupling-panels">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 340 490" role="img" aria-labelledby="flow-coupling-map-title flow-coupling-map-desc">
      <title id="flow-coupling-map-title">Affine coupling passes one group unchanged and transforms the other</title>
      <desc id="flow-coupling-map-desc">Input group u a is copied to v a. A branch takes u a to a neural network predicting log scale s and translation t. Those parameters and input group u b enter v b equals exp of s times u b elementwise plus t. The parameter networks need not themselves be invertible.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="flow-coupling-map-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="arrowhead" /></marker>
        <marker id="flow-coupling-parameter-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="accent-head" /></marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="170" y="24" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">Affine coupling: h maps u to v</text>
      <g class="node">
        <rect x="24" y="63" width="74" height="48" rx="4" />
        <rect x="244" y="63" width="74" height="48" rx="4" />
        <rect x="244" y="176" width="74" height="48" rx="4" />
        <rect x="120" y="393" width="100" height="48" rx="4" />
      </g>
      <g text-anchor="middle" class="symbol">
        <text x="61" y="94">uₐ</text><text x="281" y="94">vₐ</text>
        <text x="281" y="207">u<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">b</tspan></text>
        <text x="170" y="424">v<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">b</tspan></text>
      </g>
      <path d="M 104 87 H 238" class="forward" marker-end="url(#flow-coupling-map-arrow)" />
      <text x="171" y="72" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">copy unchanged</text>
      <rect x="24" y="161" width="144" height="78" rx="4" class="conditioner" />
      <text x="96" y="185" text-anchor="middle">s, t network</text>
      <text x="96" y="212" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">s(uₐ), t(uₐ)</text>
      <path d="M 61 117 V 155" class="forward" marker-end="url(#flow-coupling-map-arrow)" />
      <rect x="53" y="293" width="258" height="63" rx="4" class="transform" />
      <text x="182" y="319" text-anchor="middle">scale, then translate</text>
      <text x="182" y="343" text-anchor="middle" class="formula">v<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">b</tspan> = exp(s) ⊙ u<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">b</tspan> + t</text>
      <path d="M 96 245 V 266 H 128 V 287" class="parameters" marker-end="url(#flow-coupling-parameter-arrow)" />
      <text x="151" y="268" class="accent small">parameters</text>
      <path d="M 281 230 V 287" class="forward" marker-end="url(#flow-coupling-map-arrow)" />
      <path d="M 170 362 V 387" class="forward" marker-end="url(#flow-coupling-map-arrow)" />
      <text x="170" y="478" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">The s, t networks need not be invertible.</text>
    </svg>

    <svg viewBox="0 0 340 490" role="img" aria-labelledby="flow-coupling-inverse-title flow-coupling-inverse-desc">
      <title id="flow-coupling-inverse-title">Triangular Jacobian and explicit inverse of affine coupling</title>
      <desc id="flow-coupling-inverse-desc">The Jacobian has identity and zero upper blocks, an arbitrary lower-left block, and diagonal exp of s in the lower-right block. Its log absolute determinant is the sum of log scales s. Inversion first recovers u a equals v a, then recomputes s and t at v a, subtracts the translation from v b, and multiplies by exp of minus s.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="flow-coupling-inverse-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="arrowhead" /></marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="170" y="24" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">Jacobian and inverse</text>
      <text x="170" y="66" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol">J<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">h</tspan>(u)</text>
      <path d="M 53 81 H 43 V 168 H 53 M 287 81 H 297 V 168 H 287" class="bracket" />
      <text x="105" y="109" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol">I</text>
      <text x="231" y="109" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol muted">0</text>
      <text x="105" y="150" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol">∗</text>
      <text x="231" y="149" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">diag(exp(s))</text>
      <text x="170" y="196" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">∗ can be complicated; it does not enter det.</text>
      <text x="170" y="228" text-anchor="middle" class="formula accent">log |det J<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">h</tspan>| = Σⱼ sⱼ(uₐ)</text>
      <path d="M 16 254 H 324" class="divider" />
      <text x="170" y="281" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">Reverse the layer</text>
      <rect x="33" y="298" width="274" height="46" rx="4" class="node" />
      <text x="170" y="328" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol">uₐ = vₐ</text>
      <path d="M 170 350 V 392" class="forward" marker-end="url(#flow-coupling-inverse-arrow)" />
      <text x="184" y="379" class="small accent">reuse s, t</text>
      <rect x="33" y="398" width="274" height="57" rx="4" class="transform" />
      <text x="170" y="423" text-anchor="middle" class="formula">u<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">b</tspan> = (v<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">b</tspan> − t(vₐ))</text>
      <text x="170" y="446" text-anchor="middle" class="formula">⊙ exp(−s(vₐ))</text>
      <text x="170" y="478" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Subtract translation; undo the scale.</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
</NoteFigure>

<style>
  .coupling-panels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; max-width: 400px; margin-inline: auto; }
  text { fill: var(--ink); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 15px; }
  .panel-title { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; }
  .symbol { font-size: 22px; }
  .formula { font-size: 17px; }
  .subscript { font-size: 11px; }
  .small, .muted { font-size: 13px; }
  .muted { fill: var(--muted); }
  .accent { fill: var(--accent); }
  .node { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1.3; }
  .conditioner { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.3; stroke-dasharray: 4 3; }
  .transform { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.3; }
  .forward, .arrowhead { fill: none; stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .parameters, .accent-head { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .bracket { fill: none; stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .divider { stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1; }
  @container (max-width: 580px) { .coupling-panels { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; } }
</style>
